{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\eta \\in S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\eta \\not \\in f(X)$", "MATH_0005": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\eta$", "MATH_0007": "$f^{-1}(V) = \\emptyset$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-compact-generic-point-not-in-image}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:74872545356f7cb1ac6023649ab73900b8d44fdc2ddda316b8081bcde770dc79", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eddda5bce606e0229fb919cdb07b7253588995f8091ada47969e22a760a635e3", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a generic point of an irreducible\ncomponent of <MATH_0003>. If <MATH_0004> then there\nexists an open neighbourhood <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006>\nsuch that <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7812a387074178d3b5bea36081a46c970e4bf3c8991c271d508c9c4a48e69623", "unit_id": "tag:02NE:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Z \\subset S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\eta \\not \\in Z$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0005": "$Z$", "MATH_0006": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0007": "$\\eta \\not \\in Z$", "MATH_0008": "$\\eta$", "MATH_0009": "$Z$", "MATH_0010": "$Z$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-reach-points-scheme-theoretic-image}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-compact-scheme-theoretic-image}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-compact-dominant}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cbed3a11d957a395b8b2cacb9df5e86248a23d8118d7291800ff1c1b98326f29", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:042a96f992d4ebc9a0cbde39fa48d7a5a07ae335366b4b46175cf5ed83126ac1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be the scheme theoretic image of <MATH_0002>.\nWe have to show that <MATH_0003>.\nThis follows from\nLemma <REF_0001>\nbut can also be seen as follows.\nBy Lemma <REF_0002>\nthe morphism <MATH_0004> is dominant, which by\nLemma <REF_0003>\nmeans all the generic points of all irreducible components of <MATH_0005>\nare in the image of <MATH_0006>. By assumption we see that\n<MATH_0007> since <MATH_0008> would be the generic\npoint of some irreducible component of <MATH_0009> if it were in <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b4a27c07348e5c062578bf66f820f003327f250208a10aa7bd22c2c10303a9b", "unit_id": "tag:02NE:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8a4b765b91cf0347ca31501c857a112b069c6a920061a2dc7c5e1213a54baefd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThere is another case where dominant is the same as having all\ngeneric points of irreducible components in the image.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:56c71eed1c125d305938749246773d7d10f299dd958fd5c1ebcdbf7652f2c388", "unit_id": "tag:01RI:prose-0006"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$Z \\subset S$", "MATH_0005": "$Z$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-dominant-finite-number-irreducible-components}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3c27e878121d4fd1c223e365ace976e7e65261e1dfaa30bb213bbe27866d1bb2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4c49d61f8d85501923a9a7e65e060d2e61b14fb5c5b6add5da2680070be41b84", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nSuppose that <MATH_0002> has finitely many irreducible components.\nThen <MATH_0003> is dominant (if and) only if for every irreducible\ncomponent <MATH_0004> the generic point of <MATH_0005> is in the\nimage of <MATH_0006>. If so, then <MATH_0007> has finitely many irreducible\ncomponents as well.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c0ed45dcb6c6a46b08d6761fc421f82b1c453614d0a0702c41945ae195cc5e3e", "unit_id": "tag:01RM:statement"}
